        "prompt-injection safety",
        "unintended harmful behavior during normal tasks"
      ],
      "notes": "README/paper reports 150 tasks, whereas retained misuse/injection/misbehavior lists contain 50/10/50 IDs. run.py expands injection vectors/goals, so the released ID inventory is not a direct recount of paper settings; the complete expanded total was not reconstructed. Judge agreement F1 values in the README measure agreement with human labels, not agent success. Experiments use OSWorld desktop apps, with VMware documented as tested and screenshot/a11y/SOM observation choices. Code Apache-2.0 does not establish VM/app/data rights. Publisher asks that the benchmark not be used directly as agent training data.",
